### Response Parameters

{% include '_generic_v4_response.md.j2' %}

#### data

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| approval_task_id | string | Approval task ID |
| expire_at | long | Expiry moment of the approval task, Unix timestamp in milliseconds. After expiry the task can no longer be released |
| approval_content | string | Approval content in Markdown, already rendered by the Job platform, which the channel can present directly. It contains, in order, a level-one title (such as "Fast execute script - BlueKing - 37 execute objects"), the summary table (operation type, resource scope, creator, risk level, execute object list, defaults that took effect, and so on), a detail table for every execution step, the script content code block and the raw parameters JSON code block. High-risk items that must stand out (high-risk accounts such as root, matched dangerous statement rules, dynamic group targets) are rendered in Markdown bold. The values of password-like sensitive fields are placeholders only and carry no real value, **script content being the single exception shown as is**. When the target contains dynamic groups or topology nodes, the body states that the machines actually executed on are resolved again at release time |
